    "result_text": "The build passes. There's only one test class in the suite (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with a clean compile of all main sources.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration cap by mirroring the existing `CityOwnerCapacity*` validation pattern, keeping each responsibility in its own small unit:\n\n1. **`DailyRegistrationCounter`** \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals a given day (parallels `CityOwnerCounter`).\n\n2. **`DailyRegistrationCapacityValidator`** \u2014 holds the `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` cap and throws when today's count is already `>= 100` (parallels `CityOwnerCapacityValidator`).\n\n3. **`DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`** \u2014 the domain exception for the breached cap (parallels `CityOwnerCapacityExceededException`).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injects the new validator and calls `validateHasCapacity()` up front, before the other creation checks.\n\n5. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 a new handler maps `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` to **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nSince newly created owners default their `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` (via the existing `@PrePersist`) and seed owners have a null registration date, the counter naturally counts only same-day registrations: after 100 creations, the 101st is rejected with 429.",
